cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use ACTA in work you publish, please cite it.
title: "ACTA — Anybody Can Titrate Antibody"
abstract: >-
  An R workflow for analysing flow cytometry antibody titration experiments. A run reads a flowset
  of FCS files plus one Excel instructions workbook, gates positive and negative populations with
  openCyto, and reports a Stain Index per stain quantity together with a Michaelis-Menten fit, a
  PDF report, and an HTML dashboard across runs.
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/jatin199517/acta-public"
keywords:
  - flow cytometry
  - antibody titration
  - stain index
  - openCyto
  - R
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Jatin
    affiliation: "Lyell Immunopharma, Inc."

# WHEN THE PAPER IS PUBLISHED, ADD rather than REPLACE. Keep the software entry above and append a
# `preferred-citation:` block describing the article; GitHub's "Cite this repository" button then
# offers the paper while the software remains citable in its own right, which is what you want when
# someone is citing a specific version's behaviour rather than the method. Sketch:
#
#   preferred-citation:
#     type: article
#     title: "..."
#     authors: [...]
#     journal: "..."
#     year: 20XX
#     doi: "10.XXXX/..."
#
# FOR A PER-VERSION DOI, enable the GitHub-Zenodo integration BEFORE the first public release: each
# tag then mints its own DOI and the repository gets a concept DOI covering all of them. Doing it
# afterwards leaves earlier tags without one.
